## ============================================================================
## auditd FDW lab rules  ->  /etc/audit/rules.d/data.rules
## ============================================================================
## Loaded after Ubuntu's audit.rules (augenrules sorts by name), so the
## backlog settings here override the stock 8192.

## A fast generator (rotation_test.sh writes 10,000+ events in seconds) can
## overflow the kernel queue. 65536 records costs a few MB of kernel memory.
-b 65536

## When the queue is full, block the writer for up to 60 s instead of
## dropping records. Every bench run still records "lost" from auditctl -s.
--backlog_wait_time 60000

## No rate limit: lost events would be blamed on the FDW.
-r 0

## The one watch the lab is about: writes and attribute changes under /data.
## A directory watch is recursive.
-w /data -p wa -k data_watch
